Dummy Table AM
==============

This module provides two table access methods for testing the amoptions
callback and add_reloption_to_kind().  Both use heap's callbacks for
everything except reloption parsing, so their tables behave like heap
tables, except that indexes cannot be built on them: heap_getnext(),
which index builds use, accepts only heap's own TableAmRoutine.

dummy_table_am accepts all of heap's options, plus these:

  - "option_int"     (integer, -10..100)
  - "option_real"    (real, -10..100)
  - "option_bool"    (boolean)
  - "option_enum"    (enum, one|two)

Its options struct begins with StdRdOptions, and it sets
has_std_options_prefix.

dummy_custom_table_am accepts only three integer options, "option_a",
"option_b" and "option_c" (0..100, default 0).  Its options struct does
not begin with StdRdOptions, and its fields are at the offsets of
StdRdOptions' fillfactor, toast_tuple_target and toast_value_type, so
that core code wrongly reading StdRdOptions fields from it gets values
that show up in the tests.
